This README file contains information on the contents of the meta-de1soc-handoff layer.

Please see the corresponding sections below for details.

Purpose
=======

Adapts the GSRD (built for the Altera Cyclone V SoCDK) to the Terasic
DE1-SoC hardware. Two fixes, both applied automatically at build time:

1. U-Boot/SPL DDR3 handoff — the DE1-SoC DDR3 has no ECC and uses a 32-bit
   interface, unlike the SoCDK defaults. Without this patch the Yocto SPL
   hangs at DDR initialization.
2. Kernel /dev/mem access — enables the config needed for userspace mmap()
   of the HPS-FPGA bridge window (used by hps_music_player and fpga-mem-test).

No recipe from this layer is listed in IMAGE_INSTALL: both are .bbappend
files that apply automatically once the layer is registered.

Contents
========

  conf/layer.conf
  recipes-bsp/u-boot/u-boot-socfpga_v2026.01.bbappend
  recipes-bsp/u-boot/u-boot-socfpga/
      0001-DE1-SoC-disable-ECC-set-IFWIDTH-32.patch
                           Disables DDR ECC and sets IFWIDTH=32 in the
                           sdram handoff for the DE1-SoC DDR3 layout
  recipes-kernel/linux/linux-socfpga-lts_%.bbappend
  recipes-kernel/linux/linux-socfpga-lts/
      devmem.cfg           Kernel config fragment enabling unrestricted
                           /dev/mem (paired with iomem=relaxed in the
                           kernel command line)

Note on the SPL
===============

Even with the ECC/IFWIDTH patch, the most reliable DDR bring-up on the
DE1-SoC is the Terasic-provided SPL from their prebuilt image, calibrated
for the exact board DDR3 layout. The flashing procedure therefore writes
the Terasic SPL to SD partition 3 (see the build & flash guides). This
layer's U-Boot patch keeps the Yocto-built U-Boot consistent with the
board either way.

Dependencies
============

  URI: https://github.com/altera-fpga/gsrd-socfpga.git
  branch: scarthgap

  (provides the u-boot-socfpga and linux-socfpga-lts recipes that the
   .bbappend files in this layer extend)

Adding the meta-de1soc-handoff layer to your build
==================================================

Run 'bitbake-layers add-layer meta-de1soc-handoff'

Nothing else — the .bbappend files take effect on the next
'bitbake core-image-minimal'. If the GSRD bumps the U-Boot version past
v2026.01, rename the .bbappend to match (or use a % wildcard).

Patches
=======

This is a project-internal layer for the DE1-SoC FPGA Music Player
(TEC Computer Engineering). It is not submitted upstream.
